            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for glee, then the Tamil for merriment."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: வியப்பு",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வியப்பு — viyappu — \"amazement; wonder\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "குழந்தையின் திறமை எனக்கு வியப்பாக இருந்தது. kuḻantaiyiṉ tiṟamai eṉakku viyappāka iruntatu. The child’s talent amazed me."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The verb is விய \"to wonder\", with its past in -ந்த-: வியந்தேன், I marvelled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வியப்பு (viyappu) is native Dravidian, a noun from விய viya, \"to wonder, to admire\" (DEDR 5403)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
